<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram id="p_05_gaze_gates" name="05-gaze-gates"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="1049" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="Gaze: aim the head only on trustworthy evidence, through gates in a fixed order where every failed gate means HOLD STILL, because a confident wrong turn tells a group the robot is talking to someone else" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="L1" value="ATTRIBUTION&#10;who, and their bearing in ITS camera frame" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="70" width="186" height="56" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="L2" value="FACE SELECTOR&#10;hysteresis, dropout grace" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="237" y="70" width="186" height="56" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="L3" value="INTEREST LAYER&#10;what should the head do? one cell of the state matrix" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="444" y="70" width="186" height="56" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="L4" value="GAZE POLICY&#10;may I aim now? the ordered gates below" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="651" y="70" width="186" height="56" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="L5" value="HEAD CONTROLLER&#10;eased glide, nod overlay" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="858" y="70" width="186" height="56" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="L6" value="ROBOT GATEWAY&#10;frame composition, limits, the only publisher" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1065" y="70" width="186" height="56" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lay_n" value="The policy emits INTENT, never angles. Decision code is pure: driven by injected inputs and a clock, testable without a robot, camera or middleware. Whom the speech is FOR comes from the reasoner's triage verdict, not from vision." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#444444;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="130" width="1220" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g_h" value="THE GAZE POLICY: ordered gates (the order is the safety argument)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="168" width="620" height="20" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g0" value="1 STALENESS: never act on an old label" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="192" width="500" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g1" value="2 EVIDENCE: lock-eligible (mouth-motion winner, bearing-matched face, accepted by triage) / attention-only (a glance at most) / refused" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="232" width="500" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g2" value="3 SELF-SPEECH: while the robot speaks and for a tail, do not switch visitor (DoA may point at the robot); keep pursuing the locked face" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="272" width="500" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g3" value="4 SLEW HOLD: bearings taken during a head pan are the least trustworthy" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="312" width="500" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g4" value="5 DEADBAND: ignore changes under 0.05 rad [I1] (about 3 deg)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="352" width="500" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g5" value="6 DWELL: no re-aim within 2 s [I2]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="392" width="500" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g6" value="7 CONTESTED: labels alternate faster than the dwell -&gt; hold; never average two speakers" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="432" width="500" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g7" value="8 PURSUIT: follow the same locked face frame by frame; disengage on face loss" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="472" width="500" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g8" value="9 SECTOR GLANCE: off-camera directed speech, bearing stable 0.6 s [I3], robot quiet -&gt; one glance, time-boxed to 3 s [I4]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="512" width="500" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="hold" value="HOLD&#10;&#10;keep the current aim; log the suppressed decision with a reason&#10;&#10;(a gaze that does not happen is the interesting case)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="560" y="192" width="90" height="356" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="aim" value="AIM: hand an eased glide to the head controller" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="556" width="500" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="g_leg" value="green = pass, go to the next gate | red dashed = fail -&gt; HOLD. When unsure, hold still; gaze loss degrades to the old nearest-visitor gaze, never to no gaze." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#444444;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="594" width="620" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="frame" value="FRAMES. Composition rule: target yaw = MEASURED neck yaw + head-camera bearing, then clip. Using the COMMANDED yaw lets error pile up and the head 'walks away'. A bearing travels with its frame name; null, never 0, means 'no bearing'.&#10;Field of view: a face at a true 30 deg [I5] on a 90 deg camera [I6], converted linearly with a leftover 60 deg default [I7], reads 17.3 deg [I8] [calc]: the head under-turns by 12.7 deg [calc]. With the right FOV the linear formula still reads 26 deg [I9]; the pinhole form atan((x - cx) / fx) is exact (largest linear error about 4.1 deg [P10])." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="168" width="570" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="motion" value="GLIDE, NOT SACCADE. A human 40 deg saccade takes about 109 ms [P13] (21 ms + 2.2 ms per deg [P11] [P12]). The team chose not to imitate it: every move is a smoothstep glide s = 3t^2 - 2t^3, duration growing with distance, peak speed capped at 1.5 rad/s [I14]. It arrives on both axes together, with zero speed at both ends and a clean completion event. Exponential smoothing (alpha 0.1 per 50 Hz tick [I15]) reaches 95 % in about 0.57 s [I16] but never finishes cleanly." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="274" width="570" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="duty_h" value="DUTY CYCLE: share of time looking at the addressee. Plain alternation (5 s gaze [I19], 2 s away [I20]) gives 0.71 [I21] [calc]: inside the listening band, outside the speaking band." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="370" width="570" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dl_listening" value="robot design band, listening: 0.65-0.85 [I17]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="408" width="168" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="db_listening" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1108" y="414" width="77" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dh_listening" value="human 0.75 [P22]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=right;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#7b4f9e;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1035" y="434" width="110" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dl_speaking" value="robot design band, speaking: 0.35-0.55 [I18]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="448" width="168" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="db_speaking" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="991" y="454" width="78" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dh_speaking" value="human 0.41 [P23]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#7b4f9e;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1018" y="474" width="110" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dd" value="alternation 0.71" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1136" y="476" width="120" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dp0" value="0 %" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="835" y="498" width="40" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dp25" value="25 %" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="932" y="498" width="40" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dp50" value="50 %" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1030" y="498" width="40" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dp75" value="75 %" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1127" y="498" width="40" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dp100" value="100 %" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1225" y="498" width="40" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="duty_n" value="So a seeded scheduler tracks the cumulative duty and draws randomised episode lengths (people notice periodicity). Live use then moved the look-away to an eyebrow beat: a head look-away took the face out of frame and the head oscillated." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="516" width="570" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend: amber = gates and design bands | red = hold / self-speech | green = motion | blue = frames | purple ticks = public human gaze shares (the bands bracket them) | red dashed = plain alternation." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;arcSize=16;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="638" width="1220" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="sources" value="Sources. Every number is loaded from ../constants.json by the key shown. [Pn] = public (a paper, standard or physics value, or my arithmetic on one); [In] = illustrative (a round design value of the right order; never a measurement of a real robot or visitor); [calc] = my arithmetic on tagged values.&#10;Mechanism: notes/B3-gaze.md (why nearest is wrong, layers, trust, frames, arbitration, gates, the state matrix and duty cycle, motion quality, 'how it is designed and tested'). [calc]: pinhole offset (x - 0.5) = tan(30) / tan(90 / 2) / 2; linear reading = offset x FOV; under-turn = 30 - 17.3; duty = 5 / (5 + 2); asserted in the spec: 21 + 2.2 x 40 = 109 ms and ln(0.05) / ln(1 - 0.1) / 50 = 0.57 s.&#10;[I1] gaze_deadband_illustrative = 0.05 rad (about 3 deg). illustrative re-aim deadband&#10;[I2] gaze_dwell_illustrative = 2 s. illustrative minimum time between re-aims&#10;[I3] sector_glance_hold_illustrative = 0.6 s. illustrative bearing stability needed before an off-camera glance&#10;[I4] sector_glance_box_illustrative = 3 s. illustrative time box for an off-camera acquisition glance&#10;[I5] fov_example_bearing_true = 30 degrees. illustrative true bearing of a face used in the field-of-view example&#10;[I6] fov_true_illustrative = 90 degrees. illustrative true horizontal field of view of the head camera&#10;[I7] fov_default_illustrative = 60 degrees. illustrative placeholder horizontal field of view left from a development webcam&#10;[I8] fov_example_linear_wrong_fov = 17.3 degrees. illustrative: my arithmetic: pixel position of fov_example_bearing_true under a pinhole camera with fov_true_illustrative, converted back with the linear formula and fov_default_illustrative&#10;[I9] fov_example_linear_right_fov = 26 degrees. illustrative: my arithmetic: the same pixel converted with the linear formula and fov_true_illustrative&#10;[P10] linear_vs_pinhole_max_err_90 = 4.1 degrees (largest near halfway to the edge). public: my arithmetic: max over u of atan(u tan 45 deg) - 45 u deg for a 90 deg field of view&#10;[P11] saccade_duration_intercept = 21 ms. public: Carpenter, Movements of the Eyes, 1988: saccade duration ~ 21 ms + 2.2 ms per degree (main-sequence approximation; Bahill, Clark &amp; Stark 1975)&#10;[P12] saccade_duration_slope = 2.2 ms per degree. public: Carpenter 1988&#10;[P13] saccade_40deg_duration = 109 ms. public: my arithmetic from saccade_duration_intercept and saccade_duration_slope at 40 degrees&#10;[I14] head_slew_cap_illustrative = 1.5 rad/s (about 86 deg/s). illustrative peak head speed cap&#10;[I15] head_ema_alpha_illustrative = 0.1 per tick at 50 Hz. illustrative exponential smoothing of a head setpoint&#10;[I16] head_ema_t95_illustrative = 0.57 s to 95 %. illustrative: my arithmetic: ln(0.05) / ln(1 - head_ema_alpha_illustrative) / 50 Hz&#10;[I17] gaze_band_listening_illustrative = [0.65, 0.85] fraction of time looking at the addressee. illustrative design band, bracketing gaze_listener_share&#10;[I18] gaze_band_speaking_illustrative = [0.35, 0.55] fraction of time looking at the addressee. illustrative design band, bracketing gaze_speaker_share&#10;[I19] gaze_episode_mean_illustrative = 5 s. illustrative mean gaze episode&#10;[I20] lookaway_mean_illustrative = 2 s. illustrative mean look-away&#10;[I21] alternation_duty_illustrative = 0.71 fraction. illustrative: my arithmetic: gaze_episode_mean_illustrative / (gaze_episode_mean_illustrative + lookaway_mean_illustrative); inside the listening band, outside the speaking band&#10;[P22] gaze_listener_share = 0.75 fraction of listening time spent looking at the speaker. public: Argyle &amp; Ingham, 'Gaze, mutual gaze and proximity', Semiotica 6, 1972; summarised in Argyle &amp; Cook, Gaze and Mutual Gaze, 1976 (commonly cited dyadic figures)&#10;[P23] gaze_speaker_share = 0.41 fraction of speaking time spent looking at the listener. public: Argyle &amp; Ingham 1972; Argyle &amp; Cook 1976" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="678" width="1220" height="355" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="L1" target="L2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge1" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="L2" target="L3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge2" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="L3" target="L4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge3" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" source="L4" target="L5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge4" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;edgeStyle=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#666666;" edge="1" parent="1" sour